From: Artem Pelenitsyn <a.pelenitsyn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:01:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Build, install and register packages with MicroHs

Fill in the MicroHs backend of Cabal so that cabal-install can build simple
packages with mhs: a library with exposed and other modules, and executables
depending on it, in place or in the store.

MicroHs compiles a library into a single package file, and finds installed
packages through a search path of directories with an index of the modules
they provide. Cabal maps its package databases onto this as follows (see
Note [MicroHs package databases] in Distribution.Simple.MHS):

* The global database is the default search path of mhs, reported by
  'mhs -L'; its packages (base, MicroHs) are described by 'mhs -L<pkgfile>'
  and get <name>-<version> as their unit id, which is what the solver and
  'configure' then refer to.
* A database of Cabal is a directory of <unit-id>.conf registration files;
  the package file of a library stays in its build directory or, once
  installed, in its library directory.
* A component is compiled with the package files of its dependency closure
  preloaded (-p) and the search path cleared (-a), so that it sees exactly
  the packages it depends on, and a library rebuilt in place is picked up
  by its dependents without re-registration.

Executables are linked by mhs into <builddir>/<exe>/<exe>, where cabal-install
expects them, so 'cabal run' and 'cabal list-bin' work. 'Setup configure'
gains a --mhs flag, the package databases are monitored for changes, and
'cabal path' knows the compiler program.

The extensions mhs supports (all enabled at all times, CPP excepted) come
from https://github.com/augustss/MicroHs/wiki/Language.

Tested with mhs 0.16.9.0 and 0.15.4.0: cabal build/run/list-bin of a library
with a hidden module plus an executable, an up-to-date rebuild, a rebuild
after editing the hidden module, and 'cabal install' of the executable
through the store. A cabal-testsuite test covers the first of these and is
skipped when mhs is not installed.

